Chocolate Doom as a machine engine: what the game source itself must change.
Applies on top of 0001-trace-saves-bot-join.patch. Everything else the
machine needs is new code in ../i_machine.c and ../machine_doom.c.

- s_sound.c: every sound the game starts or stops goes to the platform
  (I_SoundEvent, I_StopSoundEvent) before the listener's distance decides
  whether Doom mixes it, so a host can place it for any listener. Vanilla's
  own channel logic, and its M_Random calls, are unchanged.
- s_sound.c, p_inter.c: S_StartPlayerSound. Pickup sounds, which vanilla
  plays only for the console player, go to the platform for every player,
  from that player's body; the console player's still runs vanilla's path.
- p_trace.c: TRACE_Hashes, the current state's trace record hashes, so the
  machine can be compared with native Chocolate Doom tic for tic.
- d_main.c: InitGameVersion and LoadIwadDeh lose `static`, so the machine's
  setup can call them as D_DoomMain does.

